WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:00.240 --> 00:00:05.760
A terrified man huddles in the corner, heart&nbsp;
pounding and teeth chattering. He sees them&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:00:05.760 --> 00:00:12.240
coming towards him - huge, eight-legged figures.&nbsp;
Ten feet tall, at least, with eight black,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:00:12.240 --> 00:00:18.880
soulless eyes that seem to stare hungrily at him.&nbsp;
It’s like something out of a nightmare - giant,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:00:18.880 --> 00:00:24.720
man-eating spiders, everywhere. They&nbsp;
approach the man, fangs dripping with venom,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:00:24.720 --> 00:00:29.840
but just as they’re about to strike, he&nbsp;
vanishes. He won’t be spider food today,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:00:30.400 --> 00:00:36.560
but for this truly unlucky guy, his&nbsp;
ordeal is far from over. Let’s rewind.

00:00:36.560 --> 00:00:40.880
When life gets a little too boring,&nbsp;
we all daydream about getting away.&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:00:40.880 --> 00:00:45.280
Maybe you imagine sitting on a tropical&nbsp;
beach, or camping in the mountains and&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:00:45.280 --> 00:00:50.720
breathing in the fresh air. Some of the more&nbsp;
adventurous types, with a vivid imagination,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:00:50.720 --> 00:00:56.480
might daydream about visiting a parallel universe.&nbsp;
Who wouldn’t want the chance to see what life is&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:00:56.480 --> 00:01:01.680
like in another dimension? Of course, it would&nbsp;
only be fun to go there if you could control&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:01:01.680 --> 00:01:07.760
where you went, and when you could come back.&nbsp;
Without any control over it, the ability to hop&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:01:07.760 --> 00:01:16.000
back and forth between dimensions would turn&nbsp;
from a blessing to a curse. Just ask SCP-507.
 &nbsp;

00:01:16.000 --> 00:01:24.640
SCP-507, unlike most other SCP’s, is a seemingly&nbsp;
normal human man. He has blond hair, green eyes,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:01:24.640 --> 00:01:31.200
an unrecognizable accent, and no other features&nbsp;
that might make him stand out. He looks perfectly&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:01:31.200 --> 00:01:36.560
average, like a stranger you’d pass on the street&nbsp;
and never give a second thought to. What sets him&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:01:36.560 --> 00:01:42.640
apart is not a physical attribute, but rather an&nbsp;
ability that he has yet to develop a firm grasp&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:01:42.640 --> 00:01:50.240
on. He is a dimension-hopper with no control&nbsp;
over where he goes or when he’ll get back.
 &nbsp;

00:01:50.240 --> 00:01:54.880
After appearing on the grounds of a mental&nbsp;
treatment facility with no identification,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:01:54.880 --> 00:02:02.080
rambling about a world of giant spiders, SCP-507&nbsp;
was admitted to the hospital and sedated for his&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:02:02.080 --> 00:02:07.680
own safety. He would spend several months in&nbsp;
treatment for a variety of supposed disorders,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:02:07.680 --> 00:02:13.920
but once he became aware of his surroundings, he&nbsp;
attempted to escape the hospital multiple times.

00:02:13.920 --> 00:02:19.600
During these escape attempts, he often eluded&nbsp;
hospital staff by mysteriously disappearing and&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:02:19.600 --> 00:02:25.360
reappearing in seemingly impossible places,&nbsp;
such as behind locked doors or in rooms&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:02:25.360 --> 00:02:31.280
blocked off from the rest of the hospital. These&nbsp;
disappearances and reappearances seemed to be,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:02:31.280 --> 00:02:36.640
contrary to what the hospital staff&nbsp;
first believed, beyond his control.

00:02:36.640 --> 00:02:42.320
The SCP Foundation became aware of&nbsp;
the strange phenomena surrounding 507,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:02:42.320 --> 00:02:48.240
and he was removed from the hospital and brought&nbsp;
to an SCP Foundation facility. Once there,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:02:48.240 --> 00:02:55.600
the nature of his abilities became much clearer.
 
SCP-507 is able to, without intent or even&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:02:55.600 --> 00:03:01.840
knowledge that it is about to occur, shift from&nbsp;
this reality to another, alternate reality.&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:03:01.840 --> 00:03:06.320
After some time there, with the amount&nbsp;
of time varying from case to case,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:03:06.320 --> 00:03:11.360
he will shift back to this reality. He has&nbsp;
been known to shift realities while sleeping,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:03:11.360 --> 00:03:15.760
in the middle of a sentence, and even&nbsp;
while bathing or going to the bathroom.&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:03:15.760 --> 00:03:20.560
The shifts are unpredictable, and there is no&nbsp;
telling what kind of horrors he will encounter&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:03:20.560 --> 00:03:27.200
in the new dimension where he ends up, leading&nbsp;
to 507 having seen some very strange things,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:03:27.200 --> 00:03:31.680
even by SCP Foundation Standards.
 
During one of his shifts,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:03:31.680 --> 00:03:37.200
507 found himself in a pitch-black room filled&nbsp;
with the sound of muted breathing. Using a&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:03:37.200 --> 00:03:42.400
flashlight he had been given by the Foundation,&nbsp;
he looked around and found that he was not alone.&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:03:42.400 --> 00:03:49.520
In the room with him was a man, wearing a black&nbsp;
suit and sunglasses, with a frightening, inhumanly&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:03:49.520 --> 00:03:56.720
wide smile. The Smiling Man leaned in toward&nbsp;
507, so close that their faces nearly touched,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:03:56.720 --> 00:04:04.560
and said, “Back so soon?” Terrified, 507 fired&nbsp;
several rounds from a Foundation-issued pistol,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:04:04.560 --> 00:04:09.200
then curled up in the corner of the room&nbsp;
until he shifted back to our reality.

00:04:09.200 --> 00:04:13.200
This would not be the last time&nbsp;
that he encountered the Smiling Man.&nbsp;

00:04:13.200 --> 00:04:20.400
According to Document 507-3B, which details&nbsp;
all of 507’s shifts into other realities,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:04:20.400 --> 00:04:26.720
507 was found in a Midwestern cornfield by&nbsp;
Foundation staff with brown liquid on his cheek.&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:04:26.720 --> 00:04:32.240
In his hand, he held a human heart with the&nbsp;
words “I need you” written on it in the same&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:04:32.240 --> 00:04:38.080
brown liquid. Before he shifted back, and&nbsp;
landed in the cornfield, 507 shifted to a&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:04:38.080 --> 00:04:43.200
pitch black room filled with the sound of&nbsp;
muffled crying. He turned on his flashlight,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:04:43.200 --> 00:04:49.600
taking note of his surroundings, and found himself&nbsp;
face-to-face with the Smiling Man once again.

00:04:49.600 --> 00:04:54.720
The Smiling Man had brown liquid leaking from&nbsp;
around its sunglasses, which it wiped onto&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:04:54.720 --> 00:05:02.160
507’s cheek. Upon further examination, 507 saw&nbsp;
several bullet holes in the Smiling Man’s suit,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:05:02.160 --> 00:05:07.520
leaking the same brown liquid. He attempted to&nbsp;
fire his pistol like he had the previous time,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:05:07.520 --> 00:05:14.880
but it did not fire. As the Smiling Man began to&nbsp;
approach him, 507 turned and ran. He ran for about&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:05:14.880 --> 00:05:21.440
ten minutes, before finding a corner where he&nbsp;
stayed huddled one again until he shifted back.
 &nbsp;

00:05:21.440 --> 00:05:28.080
The Smiling Man is not the only nightmare that&nbsp;
SCP-507 has encountered on his travels. During&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:05:28.080 --> 00:05:35.280
another shift, 507 described appearing in a small&nbsp;
room filled with dried corpses, a single window,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:05:35.280 --> 00:05:40.560
and a flickering light hanging from the ceiling.&nbsp;
While attempting to wait out his time in the room,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:05:40.560 --> 00:05:45.840
he discovered that the corpses were capable of&nbsp;
movement. Whenever the room was in darkness,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:05:45.840 --> 00:05:50.480
the corpses would pose themselves like&nbsp;
living people. When he looked out the window,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:05:50.480 --> 00:05:55.360
the corpses would join him and look out the&nbsp;
window with him. When he sat down, they would&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:05:55.360 --> 00:06:02.240
sit with him in a circle. 507 attempted to pass&nbsp;
time by falling asleep, but was unable to do so.
 &nbsp;

00:06:02.240 --> 00:06:08.320
Though many of his experiences were disturbing,&nbsp;
only one of 507’s documented shifts resulted in&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:06:08.320 --> 00:06:13.440
him requesting a memory wipe from the SCP&nbsp;
Foundation. On this one, he found himself&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:06:13.440 --> 00:06:19.360
in the maternity wing of a large hospital. A&nbsp;
creature, dressed like a nurse, approached 507&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:06:19.360 --> 00:06:23.920
and told him that he was “upsetting the other&nbsp;
patients,” and that it was “time to start the&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:06:23.920 --> 00:06:29.680
operation.” 507 was then wrapped in a straight&nbsp;
jacket and wheeled into an operating room.

00:06:29.680 --> 00:06:34.720
After the straight jacket was taken off, 507&nbsp;
grabbed a chair and swung it wildly at the&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:06:34.720 --> 00:06:39.920
creatures to keep them at bay until he shifted&nbsp;
back. When asked to describe the appearance of&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:06:39.920 --> 00:06:47.360
the nurse-creature, 507 began screaming in terror,&nbsp;
and was unable to provide a coherent description.&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:06:47.360 --> 00:06:52.000
He attempted to provide a drawing of the&nbsp;
creature, but was only able to produce a series&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:06:52.000 --> 00:06:58.000
of jagged lines. Following this encounter,&nbsp;
his request for a memory wipe was denied.
 &nbsp;

00:06:58.000 --> 00:07:02.000
Other shifts included going to a world&nbsp;
where every surface was covered with an&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:07:02.000 --> 00:07:07.280
unidentifiable mold, a land of icy&nbsp;
tundras populated by aggressive bears,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:07:07.280 --> 00:07:14.480
and one place that he refused to describe beyond&nbsp;
repeating the phrase “so many spiders.”  
 &nbsp;

00:07:14.480 --> 00:07:20.320
Not all of the worlds that 507 has encountered&nbsp;
are frightening. Some are simply strange and&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:07:20.320 --> 00:07:26.240
unusual. During one shift, he found himself&nbsp;
on a large basketball court, where six other&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:07:26.240 --> 00:07:31.760
individuals were playing a game of basketball.&nbsp;
There were two humans, two insectoid creatures,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:07:31.760 --> 00:07:36.880
one creature resembling a squid, and one&nbsp;
hovering yellow sphere with eight arms.

00:07:36.880 --> 00:07:43.280
When 507 asked where he was, he was informed that&nbsp;
he had arrived at the “All-species Sports Center.”

00:07:43.280 --> 00:07:48.880
During another shift, 507 found himself&nbsp;
in a world made entirely of gelatin.&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:07:48.880 --> 00:07:52.720
During yet another shift, he&nbsp;
appeared in a large auditorium&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:07:52.720 --> 00:07:57.440
filled with 50,000 other dimension-hoppers&nbsp;
who were holding a political rally for the&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:07:57.440 --> 00:08:02.720
“People’s Dimension-Hopper Republic.” Working&nbsp;
with the Republic over the course of two weeks,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:08:02.720 --> 00:08:07.280
507 helped to overthrow the United&nbsp;
States government and establish a new one&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:08:07.280 --> 00:08:14.480
run by dimension-hoppers. SCP-507 was elected&nbsp;
Representative of Massachusetts but just before&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:08:14.480 --> 00:08:20.480
he could introduce his first official piece&nbsp;
of legislation, he shifted back our reality.
 

00:08:20.480 --> 00:08:25.840
One day at the facility, a particularly&nbsp;
unusual event involving SCP-507&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:08:26.560 --> 00:08:33.600
occurred, the events of which were documented in&nbsp;
Interview 507-G. During a regular check-in, it was&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:08:33.600 --> 00:08:39.920
discovered that there were somehow two identical&nbsp;
versions of SCP-507 in its room. They had&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:08:39.920 --> 00:08:44.800
apparently each arrived in the room independently,&nbsp;
and had been talking to one another for about&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:08:44.800 --> 00:08:53.360
half an hour before being discovered. These two&nbsp;
versions were referred to as 507-A and 507-B.

00:08:53.360 --> 00:08:57.600
When prompted for an explanation,&nbsp;
507-B explained that there was more&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:08:57.600 --> 00:09:03.600
than one version of SCP-507 afflicted with&nbsp;
uncontrollable dimension-hopping. The doctor&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:09:03.600 --> 00:09:08.320
inquired as to which one of the two was the&nbsp;
visitor, but the two declined to answer,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:09:08.320 --> 00:09:13.200
fearing that this knowledge would cause the&nbsp;
Foundation to view one of them as expendable.
 &nbsp;

00:09:13.200 --> 00:09:18.160
The two had multiple shared experiences that&nbsp;
they related to the doctor, including both&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:09:18.160 --> 00:09:24.720
having encounters with the Smiling Man. During&nbsp;
the interview, 507-B disappeared mid-sentence&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:09:24.720 --> 00:09:31.040
and did not reappear. The doctor asked 507-A&nbsp;
about identifiable differences between his&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:09:31.040 --> 00:09:37.760
and his double’s realities. 507-A explained&nbsp;
that in 507-B’s world, President Lincoln&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:09:37.760 --> 00:09:43.920
was killed by his vice-president, whereas in&nbsp;
507-A’s world he was killed by General Lee.

00:09:43.920 --> 00:09:52.080
This revelation made it clear that neither 507-A&nbsp;
nor 507-B were native to this reality. After this&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:09:52.080 --> 00:10:00.480
was revealed, 507-A was terminated and examined.&nbsp;
No biological reason for 507’s ability to hop from&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:10:00.480 --> 00:10:06.480
dimension to dimension was found, though it was&nbsp;
discovered that severed pieces of 507 will shift&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:10:06.480 --> 00:10:11.600
dimensions along with the rest of the body.&nbsp;
Three days after this interview was conducted,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:10:11.600 --> 00:10:18.560
the correct SCP-507 reappeared, with no knowledge&nbsp;
of his doppelgangers or what became of them.
 &nbsp;

00:10:18.560 --> 00:10:24.800
SCP-507 is classified as “safe,” meaning he&nbsp;
doesn’t require any real effort to contain.&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:10:24.800 --> 00:10:30.240
He’s also safe in the more literal sense,&nbsp;
in that he poses no threat to anyone else.&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:10:30.240 --> 00:10:35.680
The only person in danger in the&nbsp;
presence of SCP-507 is himself,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:10:35.680 --> 00:10:40.480
as he has been exposed to many dangerous&nbsp;
conditions during his reality shifts,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:10:40.480 --> 00:10:46.160
and it is never known whether 507’s&nbsp;
next shift will end up being his last.

00:10:46.160 --> 00:10:50.880
With the cause of his shifts still being unknown,&nbsp;
there is nothing that the Foundation can do&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:10:50.880 --> 00:10:56.800
to prevent them. All that they can do is monitor&nbsp;
him, and provide him with items that might ensure&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:10:56.800 --> 00:11:02.240
his safety in the future, like a handgun&nbsp;
loaded with rubber bullets, a tank of air,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:11:02.240 --> 00:11:08.560
a high-intensity flashlight, a week of ration&nbsp;
packs, a pair of binoculars, a tracking collar,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:11:08.560 --> 00:11:14.080
and a camera. The tracking collar allows the&nbsp;
Foundation to recover 507 when he shifts back&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:11:14.080 --> 00:11:19.760
to our reality in a location other than the&nbsp;
containment facility. The rest of the equipment&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:11:19.760 --> 00:11:25.760
was granted at his request, based on obstacles&nbsp;
that he encountered in other dimensions.
 &nbsp;

00:11:25.760 --> 00:11:31.920
Due to his docile nature, 507 is given freedom&nbsp;
to move about the facility, but when he leaves&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:11:31.920 --> 00:11:37.120
his private room, an agent must go with him&nbsp;
to document any shifts that might occur.&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:11:37.120 --> 00:11:43.360
No one is allowed to touch SCP-507 though, if&nbsp;
it has been more than two weeks since a shift&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:11:43.360 --> 00:11:48.560
occurred. This policy stems from an incident&nbsp;
in which an agent who was touching 507’s&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:11:48.560 --> 00:11:53.440
shoulder at the time of a shift was&nbsp;
taken with him… and did not return.

00:11:53.440 --> 00:11:59.760
When he is not shifting, SCP-507 lives a&nbsp;
relatively normal life at the facility. He&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:11:59.760 --> 00:12:06.480
is allowed his own computer with internet access,&nbsp;
and can meet with other Safe or Euclid-class SCPs&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:12:06.480 --> 00:12:12.320
that are not infectious or detrimental to his&nbsp;
health. 507 has expressed an interest in the&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:12:12.320 --> 00:12:18.400
unusual and paranormal, and has enjoyed meeting&nbsp;
with other SCP’s, including a request to visit&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:12:18.400 --> 00:12:26.080
SCP-082 for a “vacation.” So far, all of&nbsp;
these meetings have occurred without incident.&nbsp;

00:12:26.080 --> 00:12:33.200
Due to his anomalous shifting, SCP-507 will&nbsp;
never be able to live a normal life. Unless&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:12:33.200 --> 00:12:38.080
he stops shifting, he will likely spend the&nbsp;
rest of his days bouncing between unknown&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:12:38.080 --> 00:12:43.120
dimensions and his containment facility.&nbsp;
Just like so much else about him,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:12:43.120 --> 00:12:49.360
his relationship to his special talent is a bit&nbsp;
of a paradox. He has the ability to go anywhere,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:12:49.360 --> 00:12:55.520
to see things no other person on this earth has&nbsp;
ever seen. However, because he cannot control it,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:12:55.520 --> 00:13:02.000
cannot stop it, no matter how far away he&nbsp;
can travel, he will never be truly free.

00:13:02.000 --> 00:13:05.120
Now go check out “SCP - 1000 - Bigfoot”&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:13:05.120 --> 00:13:11.760
and “SCP - 066 - Eric’s Toy” for more&nbsp;
tragic tales from the SCP Foundation.

